<title>JAPAN: Tokyo corn futures market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo corn futures market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo corn futures market is closed on Monday due for a national holiday. Trading will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, the market closed lower in all months as price drops in the Chicago corn market overnight triggered active selling, traders said. Prices were 150 to 470 yen lower, with the benchmark November 1997 contract down 180 yen at 13,950 yen a tonne.</p>
</text>
